mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>The treatment of breast diseases in women of reproductive age requires not only a focus on therapeutic efficacy but also a comprehensive consideration of factors such as breast aesthetics, reproductive endocrinology, humanistic and ethical dimensions, and physiological states related to menstruation and pregnancy. This course covers physiological anatomy, advances in the diagnosis and treatment of benign and malignant diseases, plastic surgery and aesthetics, genetic counseling, hormone replacement therapy, breast cancer during pregnancy, humanistic ethics, as well as integrated traditional Chinese and Western medicine approaches. It is highly beneficial for enhancing interest, broadening knowledge, and informing future career direction choices.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
